Subject: [PATCH 1/2] =?UTF-8?q?safe-commands:=20with=20no=20task,=20an=20a?=
 =?UTF-8?q?lias=20gets=20its=20target's=20verdict=20=E2=80=94=20fw=20fix-l?=
 =?UTF-8?q?earned,=20fw=20git=20commit=20(from=20832=20T-650/T-1037;=20AEF?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20T-3814)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The completion prompt prints `fw fix-learned T-XXX "..."` and `fw git commit -m "..."`, and with
no active task (the state every completion leaves) the gate refused both, while their targets,
`fw context add-learning` and bare `git commit`, are admitted. An allowlist of effects must not be
indexed by spelling.
- `fix-learned` joins the fw no-task allowlist (bin/fw execs `context add-learning` for it).
- `_fw_is_git_commit_clause` treats `fw git commit` as `git commit`, for the real fw spellings only:
  `fw`, `bin/fw`, `.agentic-framework/bin/fw`, an absolute `.../.agentic-framework/bin/fw`. A planted
  `/tmp/x/bin/fw` is refused. Every is_commit_checkpoint_command guard still applies
  (substitution, --no-verify/-n, write patterns, per-clause safety).
Probe: tests/unit/test_t1040_alias_is_its_target.sh (+ _t1040_mutation_assert.sh). On v1.8.0: 10/16.
On v1.8.0 + bundle D: 16/16 after this commit; without D it is 15/16, because the prose-argument
leg needs D's _sc_is_framework_prose_verb. Apply after bundle D.
Unchanged before and after (v1.8.0 + D as the baseline): check_active_task.bats,
test_pretooluse_gates.bats (6, 12 fail on both), context_safe_commands.bats (42 fails on both),
and 7 more safe-commands suites (all ok).
